              "presentation": "core",
              "title": "以 still 詢問未改變的狀態",
              "sourceCueIds": [
                "c1"
              ],
              "contextCueIds": [],
              "explanation": "「still」在此處表示「仍然、還」。在疑問句「Why are you still here?」中，用來詢問某個狀態為何至今尚未改變，語氣中常帶有原以為對方已離開或事情已結束的意外感。",
              "sourceSpans": [
                {
                  "cueId": "c1",
                  "start": 12,
                  "end": 17
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "cbfdc81c-4b88-4345-95e3-5f2be182deb8:s0:p2",
              "utteranceIds": [
                "449207b1-0233-455b-8f47-9af0bce73e7c"
              ],
              "category": "grammar",
              "presentation": "core",
              "title": "was about to 表示過去正準備做某事",
              "sourceCueIds": [
                "c2"
              ],
              "contextCueIds": [],
              "explanation": "「be about to + 原形動詞」表示正打算或即將做某事。句中使用過去式「was about to leave」，表示在過去另一個動作發生（即「when you called」來電）的那個時間點，說話者剛好正準備離開。",
              "sourceSpans": [
                {
                  "cueId": "c2",
                  "start": 2,
                  "end": 20
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "cbfdc81c-4b88-4345-95e3-5f2be182deb8:s0:p3",
              "utteranceIds": [
                "021756d5-1736-4838-bb51-af0a5b1fdb45"
              ],
